ity-related entanglement", "parentId": "grav-quantum", "level": 2, "summary": "Proposals need a declared mediator model and nongravitational controls.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-q-entangle", "grav-src-2026-1", "grav-src-2026-2"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-witness"><data key="title">Witness assumptions and alternatives</data><data key="kind">topic</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">mapped</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-witness", "title": "Witness assumptions and alternatives", "parentId": "grav-entangle", "level": 3, "summary": "An entanglement witness is not automatically a model-independent quantum-gravity certificate.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-q-entangle", "grav-src-2026-1", "grav-src-2026-2"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-strings"><data key="title">String theory and holography</data><data key="kind">topic</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">mapped</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-strings", "title": "String theory and holography", "parentId": "grav-quantum", "level": 2, "summary": "Controlled dualities have specified spacetime and large-N regimes.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-ads"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-ads"><data key="title">AdS/CFT regimes</data><data key="kind">topic</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">mapped</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-ads", "title": "AdS/CFT regimes", "parentId": "grav-strings", "level": 3, "summary": "A selected conjectured correspondence is not a measured cosmological model.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-ads"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-loops"><data key="title">Loop quantum gravity</data><data key="kind">topic</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">mapped</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-loops", "title": "Loop quantum gravity", "parentId": "grav-quantum", "level": 2, "summary": "Kinematical spectra and physical-dynamics recovery are distinct obligations.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-lqg"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-area"><data key="title">Area/volume spectra</data><data key="kind">topic</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">mapped</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-area", "title": "Area/volume spectra", "parentId": "grav-loops", "level": 3, "summary": "Representation-level results do not alone establish observed Planck discreteness.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-lqg"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-obligations"><data key="title">Continuum and empirical obligations</data><data key="kind">topic</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">mapped</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-obligations", "title": "Continuum and empirical obligations", "parentId": "grav-quantum", "level": 2, "summary": "Recover GR, matter, observables and testable departures in a specified regime.", "coverage": "mapped", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "prerequisites": [], "formulaIds": [], "kind": "topic", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-force"><data key="title">Newtonian two-body attraction</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-force", "topicId": "grav-forces", "title": "Newtonian two-body attraction", "latex": "\\mathbf F_{1\\leftarrow2}=-GMm\\,\\mathbf r/r^3", "plain": "The separation vector points from source M to test mass m; the minus sign makes attraction.", "variables": [{"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "m", "meaning": "Test mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Source-to-test separation vector; scalar r in denominator is its positive Euclidean norm", "unit": "m", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "F", "meaning": "Force on test mass", "unit": "N", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "U", "meaning": "Newtonian interaction potential energy introduced in derivation", "unit": "J", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Point masses or exterior spherical source", "Nonrelativistic isolated interaction"], "derivation": ["Rotational symmetry fixes a radial force.", "Potential U=-GMm/r gives F=-grad U."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"M_kg": 1, "m_kg": 1, "r_m": 1}, "steps": ["Insert measured G=6.67430e-11 SI.", "The force points toward the source."], "result": "6.67430e-11 N inward", "units": "N"}, "limitingCases": ["M=0 gives zero force"], "pitfalls": ["At r=0 the point model is singular; an extended density must replace it."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-field"><data key="title">Acceleration field</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-field", "topicId": "grav-forces", "title": "Acceleration field", "latex": "\\mathbf g=-GM\\mathbf r/r^3", "plain": "Test-body acceleration is force divided by inertial mass under equality of inertial and passive gravitational mass.", "variables": [{"symbol": "g", "meaning": "Gravitational acceleration", "unit": "m s^-2", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Separation vector; scalar r in denominator is its positive Euclidean norm", "unit": "m", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Test mass does not appreciably perturb source", "Universal coupling assumed"], "derivation": ["Divide Newton force by m.", "The test mass cancels algebraically."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"M_kg": 5.9722e+24, "r_m": 6371000.0}, "steps": ["Compute GM/r^2.", "Ignore rotation, oblateness and altitude."], "result": "Approximately9.82 m/s² inward", "units": "m s^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Far from source magnitude tends to zero"], "pitfalls": ["Mass cancellation in the model is not an experimental proof of universal free fall."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-potential"><data key="title">Potential and conservative acceleration</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-potential", "topicId": "grav-potential", "title": "Potential and conservative acceleration", "latex": "\\Phi=-GM/r,\\quad\\mathbf g=-\\nabla\\Phi", "plain": "Potential is energy per unit test mass, fixed here to zero at infinity.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Phi", "meaning": "Gravitational potential", "unit": "m^2 s^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Radial distance", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "g", "meaning": "Acceleration", "unit": "m s^-2", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "nabla", "meaning": "Spatial gradient", "unit": "m^-1", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Static isolated spherical source", "Zero potential at infinity"], "derivation": ["Integrate -GM/r² radially with boundary Phi(infinity)=0.", "Differentiate to recover acceleration."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_SI": 398600441800000.0, "r_m": 7000000.0}, "steps": ["Evaluate -GM/r.", "Its gradient, not its arbitrary additive constant, affects acceleration."], "result": "-5.69429e7 m²/s²", "units": "m² s^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Adding a constant leaves g unchanged"], "pitfalls": ["Do not identify a coordinate potential value with a directly measured absolute energy."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-poisson"><data key="title">Poisson equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-poisson", "topicId": "grav-potential", "title": "Poisson equation", "latex": "\\nabla^2\\Phi=4\\pi G\\rho", "plain": "Mass density sources a Newtonian potential through a boundary-value problem.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Phi", "meaning": "Potential", "unit": "m^2 s^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "rho", "meaning": "Mass density", "unit": "kg m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "nabla^2", "meaning": "Spatial Laplacian", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Newtonian static or instantaneous approximation", "Boundary conditions specified", "Classical pointwise equation requires sufficient potential/source regularity; point masses and surface layers require a distributional interpretation at the singularsupport."], "derivation": ["Use Gauss divergence theorem with flux integral of g=-4piG enclosed mass.", "Set g=-grad Phi."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"rho_kg_m3": 1000}, "steps": ["Compute4piG rho.", "Both sides have dimension s^-2."], "result": "8.38717e-7 s^-2", "units": "s^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Vacuum has LaplacianPhi=0, not necessarily zero field"], "pitfalls": ["A harmonic potential can be nonzero; source equation without boundaries is not unique.", "For Phi=-GM/r, the Laplacian vanishes only off r=0; distributionally it equals4piGM delta3 at the origin. No automaticglobalC2regularity follows from writing the equation."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-escape"><data key="title">Escape speed</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-escape", "topicId": "grav-escape", "title": "Escape speed", "latex": "v_{esc}=\\sqrt{2GM/r}", "plain": "Zero energy at infinity determines the ideal minimum launch speed.", "variables": [{"symbol": "v_esc", "meaning": "Escape speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Initial radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["No atmosphere or other bodies", "Newtonian point/exterior spherical source"], "derivation": ["Set specific energy v²/2-GM/r to zero.", "Solve positive speed."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_SI": 398600441800000.0, "r_m": 6371000.0}, "steps": ["Compute sqrt(2GM/r).", "Exclude Earth rotation."], "result": "Approximately11.186 km/s", "units": "m s^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["As r increases escape speed decreases"], "pitfalls": ["A local escape estimate neglects later thrust, drag and other gravitating bodies."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-circular"><data key="title">Circular orbital speed</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-circular", "topicId": "grav-escape", "title": "Circular orbital speed", "latex": "v_c=\\sqrt{GM/r}", "plain": "Centripetal acceleration equals gravitational acceleration for an ideal circular orbit.", "variables": [{"symbol": "v_c", "meaning": "Circular speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Orbital radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Test-body circular orbit", "Newtonian weak field"], "derivation": ["Set v²/r=GM/r².", "Take positive magnitude."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_SI": 398600441800000.0, "r_m": 7000000.0}, "steps": ["Compute sqrt(GM/r).", "Compare escape speed at the same radius."], "result": "7546.05 m/s", "units": "m s^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["v_esc=sqrt2 v_c"], "pitfalls": ["Using altitude as radius instead of centre distance produces a large error."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-kepler"><data key="title">Kepler period</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-kepler", "topicId": "grav-kepler", "title": "Kepler period", "latex": "T^2=4\\pi^2a^3/[G(M+m)]", "plain": "The relative two-body ellipse has a period determined by semimajor axis and total mass.", "variables": [{"symbol": "T", "meaning": "Period", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Relative semimajor axis", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M,m", "meaning": "Two masses", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Isolated bound Newtonian two-body system", "Ellipse with0&lt;=e&lt;1"], "derivation": ["Use angular-momentum conservation and ellipse area.", "Insert the inverse-square orbit relation."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"a_m": 149597870700.0, "GMtotal_SI": 1.3271244e+20}, "steps": ["Compute2pi sqrt(a³/GMtotal).", "Round illustrative inputs."], "result": "Approximately365.26 days", "units": "s"}, "limitingCases": ["Circular limit preserves same period at radiusa"], "pitfalls": ["A planet perturbation or relativistic precession violates an exactly closed Kepler ellipse."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-visviva"><data key="title">Vis-viva relation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-visviva", "topicId": "grav-energy", "title": "Vis-viva relation", "latex": "v^2=G(M+m)(2/r-1/a)", "plain": "Instantaneous speed follows orbital energy; a is signed for hyperbolic convention.", "variables": [{"symbol": "v", "meaning": "Relative speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M,m", "meaning": "Masses", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Separation", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Semimajor axis", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Newtonian two-body potential", "a&gt;0 for ellipse and a&lt;0 for hyperbola"], "derivation": ["Specific energy is-G(M+m)/(2a).", "Equate to v²/2-G(M+m)/r."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_SI": 1, "r_m": 1, "a_m": 1}, "steps": ["Substitute into2/r-1/a.", "This is a scaled mathematical example."], "result": "v=1 m/s", "units": "m s^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["a→infinity recovers parabolic escape"], "pitfalls": ["Not every numerical r,a pair is consistent with a physical orbit and angular momentum."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-specificenergy"><data key="title">Specific mechanical energy</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-specificenergy", "topicId": "grav-energy", "title": "Specific mechanical energy", "latex": "\\epsilon=v^2/2-GM/r", "plain": "Energy per unit test mass separates bound, parabolic and unbound Newtonian motion.", "variables": [{"symbol": "epsilon", "meaning": "Specific energy", "unit": "J kg^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "v", "meaning": "Speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Static point potential", "Negligible dissipation"], "derivation": ["Divide kinetic plus potential energy by test mass.", "Use potential zero at infinity."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_SI": 1, "r_m": 1, "v_m_s": 1}, "steps": ["Compute1/2-1.", "Negative energy permits bound motion."], "result": "-0.5 J/kg", "units": "J kg^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["epsilon=0 marks parabolic energy"], "pitfalls": ["Negative energy does not specify a unique ellipse without angular momentum."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-angular"><data key="title">Specific angular momentum</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-angular", "topicId": "grav-orbits", "title": "Specific angular momentum", "latex": "\\mathbf h=\\mathbf r\\times\\mathbf v", "plain": "A central force conserves the orbital plane and areal velocity.", "variables": [{"symbol": "h", "meaning": "Specific angular momentum", "unit": "m^2 s^-1", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Relative displacement", "unit": "m", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "v", "meaning": "Relative velocity", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "vector"}], "conditions": ["Central force", "No external torque"], "derivation": ["Differentiate r×v.", "Both v×v and r×radial acceleration vanish."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"r_m": [1, 0, 0], "v_m_s": [0, 2, 0]}, "steps": ["Take the cross product.", "The z component is positive."], "result": "h=(0,0,2) m²/s", "units": "m² s^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["Pure radial motion has h=0"], "pitfalls": ["A nongravitational torque breaks conservation even if gravity remains central."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-tidal"><data key="title">Point-mass tidal tensor</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-tidal", "topicId": "grav-tidal", "title": "Point-mass tidal tensor", "latex": "\\delta a_i={GM\\over r^3}(3n_i n_j-\\delta_{ij})\\xi_j", "plain": "Nearby free bodies separate radially and compress transversely in this Newtonian vacuum field.", "variables": [{"symbol": "delta a_i", "meaning": "Relative acceleration", "unit": "m s^-2", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Reference radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Source mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "n_i", "meaning": "Radial unit vector components", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "delta_ij", "meaning": "Kronecker identity", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "xi_j", "meaning": "Small separation components", "unit": "m", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "i,j", "meaning": "Cartesian component indices1..3", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Separation much smaller than r", "Einstein sum over repeated j"], "derivation": ["Linearize g at displaced position.", "Differentiate g=-GM r/r³; radial eigenvalue is2GM/r³."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_over_r3_s2": 1, "xi_radial_m": 0.01}, "steps": ["Apply the radial eigenvalue2.", "The transverse eigenvalues are-1."], "result": "Radial deltaa=0.02 m/s²", "units": "m s^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Trace vanishes outside source"], "pitfalls": ["A uniform local acceleration can be transformed away; a tidal tensor generally cannot."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-hydro"><data key="title">Spherical hydrostatic balance</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-hydro", "topicId": "grav-hydro", "title": "Spherical hydrostatic balance", "latex": "{dp\\over dr}=-{GM(r)\\rho(r)\\over r^2}", "plain": "In a stationary Newtonian fluid, pressure decreases outward to oppose gravity.", "variables": [{"symbol": "p", "meaning": "Pressure", "unit": "Pa", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M(r)", "meaning": "Enclosed mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "rho", "meaning": "Mass density", "unit": "kg m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Spherical static fluid", "Newtonian pressure small relative to rest energy density"], "derivation": ["Balance pressure force on a thin shell with gravitational force.", "Take shell thickness to zero."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"g_m_s2": 10, "rho_kg_m3": 1000}, "steps": ["Use local g=GM(r)/r².", "Multiply-rho g."], "result": "dp/dr=-10000 Pa/m", "units": "Pa m^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["Zero density yields zero pressure gradient"], "pitfalls": ["Compact stars require relativistic TOV and an equation of state, not this equation."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-radius"><data key="title">Schwarzschild length</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-radius", "topicId": "grav-schwarzschild", "title": "Schwarzschild length", "latex": "r_s=2GM/c^2", "plain": "A mass defines the Schwarzschild horizon radius only for the stated nonrotating vacuum solution.", "variables": [{"symbol": "r_s", "meaning": "Schwarzschild radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Mass parameter", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Nonrotating uncharged Schwarzschild spacetime", "Do not infer a horizon from density alone"], "derivation": ["Solve1-2GM/(rc²)=0 in Schwarzschild metric.", "This identifies a coordinate-horizon surface in the solution."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"M_kg": 1.98847e+30}, "steps": ["Insert solar mass and SI constants.", "Round numerical inputs."], "result": "Approximately2953.34 m", "units": "m"}, "limitingCases": ["r_s scales linearly with M"], "pitfalls": ["An ordinary star with radius much larger than r_s is not a black hole."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-interval"><data key="title">Spacetime interval</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-interval", "topicId": "grav-metric", "title": "Spacetime interval", "latex": "ds^2=g_{\\mu\\nu}dx^\\mu dx^\\nu", "plain": "A metric contracts coordinate displacements into an invariant interval.", "variables": [{"symbol": "ds²", "meaning": "Squared interval", "unit": "m^2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "g_munu", "meaning": "Metric components; units depend on chart", "unit": "chart-dependent", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "dx^mu", "meaning": "Coordinate displacement", "unit": "chart-dependent", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "mu,nu", "meaning": "Spacetime indices0..3; repeated summed", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Signature(-,+,+,+)", "x0=ct; all four Cartesian coordinates measured in metres"], "derivation": ["Apply the bilinear metric to a tangent displacement twice.", "Under a coordinate change the component factors transform oppositely."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"c_dt_m": 5, "dx_m": 3, "dy_m": 0, "dz_m": 0}, "steps": ["Use Minkowski diag(-1,1,1,1).", "Compute-25+9."], "result": "ds²=-16 m², timelike", "units": "m²"}, "limitingCases": ["Null displacement has ds²=0"], "pitfalls": ["In spherical coordinates angular components have different coordinate units; metric entries are not all dimensionless there."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-propertime"><data key="title">Timelike proper time</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-propertime", "topicId": "grav-metric", "title": "Timelike proper time", "latex": "d\\tau=\\sqrt{-ds^2}/c", "plain": "An ideal comoving clock measures proper time along a timelike worldline.", "variables": [{"symbol": "tau", "meaning": "Proper time", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "ds²", "meaning": "Squared interval", "unit": "m²", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Timelike path", "Metric signature(-,+,+,+)"], "derivation": ["Normalize the tangent four-velocity.", "Rearrange ds²=-c²dτ²."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"ds2_m2": -9}, "steps": ["Take sqrt9 metres.", "Divide by c."], "result": "dτ≈1.00069e-8 s", "units": "s"}, "limitingCases": ["A null path has zero proper time but no rest-frame photon clock"], "pitfalls": ["Spacelike intervals do not define real elapsed proper time by this formula."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-connection"><data key="title">Levi-Civita connection</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-connection", "topicId": "grav-connection", "title": "Levi-Civita connection", "latex": "\\Gamma^\\rho_{\\mu\\nu}={1\\over2}g^{\\rho\\sigma}(\\partial_\\mu g_{\\sigma\\nu}+\\partial_\\nu g_{\\sigma\\mu}-\\partial_\\sigma g_{\\mu\\nu})", "plain": "Metric compatibility and zero torsion uniquely fix this connection.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Gamma", "meaning": "Connection coefficients", "unit": "m^-1 in length coordinates", "kind": "coordinate"}, {"symbol": "g^rhosigma", "meaning": "Inverse metric", "unit": "dimensionless in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "g_munu", "meaning": "Metric", "unit": "dimensionless in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "partial", "meaning": "Coordinate derivative", "unit": "m^-1", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "rho,mu,nu,sigma", "meaning": "Indices0..3; repeated sigma summed", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Smooth nondegenerate metric", "Torsion-free metric connection"], "derivation": ["Write covariant derivative of g equal to zero.", "Permute three index equations and solve for Gamma."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"metric": "Constant Cartesian Minkowski"}, "steps": ["Every metric derivative vanishes.", "Insert into connection formula."], "result": "All Gamma components vanish", "units": "m^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["Curvilinear flat coordinates can have nonzero Gamma"], "pitfalls": ["Gamma is not a tensor; nonzero coefficients alone do not establish curvature."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-geodesic"><data key="title">Affine geodesic equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-geodesic", "topicId": "grav-geodesic", "title": "Affine geodesic equation", "latex": "{d^2x^\\mu\\over d\\tau^2}+\\Gamma^\\mu_{\\alpha\\beta}{dx^\\alpha\\over d\\tau}{dx^\\beta\\over d\\tau}=0", "plain": "A freely falling test body has zero covariant four-acceleration.", "variables": [{"symbol": "x^mu", "meaning": "Worldline coordinates", "unit": "m in length chart", "kind": "coordinate"}, {"symbol": "tau", "meaning": "Timelike proper time", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "Gamma", "meaning": "Connection coefficients", "unit": "m^-1", "kind": "coordinate"}, {"symbol": "mu,alpha,beta", "meaning": "Indices0..3; repeated indices summed", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "A^mu", "meaning": "Constant tangent in flat-worldline example", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "B^mu", "meaning": "Constant initial position in flat-worldline example", "unit": "m", "kind": "vector"}], "conditions": ["Timelike test body", "No nongravitational force", "Proper time is affine"], "derivation": ["Extremize proper-time action or parallel transport tangent.", "Expand covariant derivative along the curve."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Gamma": "0 in Cartesian Minkowski"}, "steps": ["Connection term vanishes.", "Integrate d²x/dτ²=0."], "result": "x^mu=A^mu τ+B^mu", "units": "m"}, "limitingCases": ["A coordinate acceleration need not vanish in curved coordinates"], "pitfalls": ["Accelerated rockets and extended spinning bodies need additional force or multipole equations."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-riemann"><data key="title">Curvature sign convention</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-riemann", "topicId": "grav-riemann", "title": "Curvature sign convention", "latex": "R^\\rho{}_{\\sigma\\mu\\nu}=\\partial_\\mu\\Gamma^\\rho_{\\nu\\sigma}-\\partial_\\nu\\Gamma^\\rho_{\\mu\\sigma}+\\Gamma^\\rho_{\\mu\\lambda}\\Gamma^\\lambda_{\\nu\\sigma}-\\Gamma^\\rho_{\\nu\\lambda}\\Gamma^\\lambda_{\\mu\\sigma}", "plain": "Curvature measures failure of covariant derivatives to commute under the declared sign.", "variables": [{"symbol": "R", "meaning": "Riemann components", "unit": "m^-2 in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "Gamma", "meaning": "Connection", "unit": "m^-1", "kind": "coordinate"}, {"symbol": "partial", "meaning": "Coordinate derivative", "unit": "m^-1", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "rho,sigma,mu,nu,lambda", "meaning": "Indices0..3; lambda summed", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Smooth torsion-free connection", "This sign convention fixes Ricci and Einstein signs"], "derivation": ["Apply[∇mu,∇nu] to a vector.", "Collect derivative and quadratic connection terms."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Gamma": "0 everywhere in Cartesian Minkowski"}, "steps": ["All derivatives and products are zero.", "A coordinate change cannot change vanishing curvature."], "result": "R=0", "units": "m^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Vanishing Gamma at one point does not force derivatives to vanish"], "pitfalls": ["Opposite Riemann conventions require coordinated sign changes; do not mix textbooks silently."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-ricci"><data key="title">Ricci and scalar curvature</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-ricci", "topicId": "grav-riemann", "title": "Ricci and scalar curvature", "latex": "R_{\\sigma\\nu}=R^\\rho{}_{\\sigma\\rho\\nu},\\quad R=g^{\\sigma\\nu}R_{\\sigma\\nu}", "plain": "Contractions summarize only part of the curvature tensor.", "variables": [{"symbol": "R_sigmanu", "meaning": "Ricci tensor", "unit": "m^-2 in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "R^rho_sigmamunu", "meaning": "Riemann tensor", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "R", "meaning": "Scalar curvature", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "g^sigmanu", "meaning": "Inverse metric", "unit": "dimensionless in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "rho,sigma,nu", "meaning": "Indices0..3; repeated summed", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Same curvature sign as grav-f-riemann", "Nondegenerate metric"], "derivation": ["Trace first and third Riemann slots.", "Contract Ricci with inverse metric."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"spacetime": "Schwarzschild vacuum outside source"}, "steps": ["Vacuum Einstein equation without Lambda gives Ricci zero.", "Weyl curvature remains nonzero."], "result": "Ricci=0 and scalarR=0; full curvature need not vanish", "units": "m^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Minkowski has full curvature zero"], "pitfalls": ["Ricci-flat does not mean gravity-free; black-hole tidal curvature is a counterexample."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-einstein"><data key="title">Einstein field equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-einstein", "topicId": "grav-einstein", "title": "Einstein field equation", "latex": "R_{\\mu\\nu}-{1\\over2}Rg_{\\mu\\nu}+\\Lambda g_{\\mu\\nu}={8\\pi G\\over c^4}T_{\\mu\\nu}", "plain": "Local stress energy and spacetime curvature are related by a nonlinear metric equation.", "variables": [{"symbol": "R_munu", "meaning": "Ricci tensor", "unit": "m^-2 in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "R", "meaning": "Scalar curvature", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "g_munu", "meaning": "Metric", "unit": "dimensionless in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "Lambda", "meaning": "Cosmological constant", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "T_munu", "meaning": "Stress-energy components in orthonormal SI frame", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "mu,nu", "meaning": "Indices0..3", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Signature(-,+,+,+) and declared curvature sign", "Classical metric and specified matter", "Gauge and initial/boundary data required"], "derivation": ["Vary Einstein-Hilbert plus matter action.", "Discard/compensate boundary variations with a consistent boundary prescription."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Lambda": 0, "matter": "Vacuum Minkowski"}, "steps": ["T=0 and full curvature0.", "Both sides vanish."], "result": "0=0", "units": "m^-2 on both sides"}, "limitingCases": ["Newtonian weak-field limit recovers Poisson with appropriate matter"], "pitfalls": ["Ten component equations include constraint/gauge structure; arbitrary metric components are not ten independent physical waves."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-fluid"><data key="title">Perfect-fluid stress energy</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-fluid", "topicId": "grav-matter", "title": "Perfect-fluid stress energy", "latex": "T^{\\mu\\nu}=(\\varepsilon+p)u^\\mu u^\\nu/c^2+p g^{\\mu\\nu}", "plain": "Energy density and isotropic pressure are defined in the fluid rest frame.", "variables": [{"symbol": "T^munu", "meaning": "Stress energy", "unit": "J m^-3 in orthonormal frame", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "epsilon", "meaning": "Rest-frame total energy density", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "p", "meaning": "Isotropic pressure", "unit": "Pa", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "u^mu", "meaning": "Four velocity", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "vector"}, {"symbol": "g^munu", "meaning": "Inverse metric", "unit": "dimensionless in orthonormal frame", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "mu,nu", "meaning": "Indices0..3", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Local equilibrium and isotropic stress", "u·u=-c²", "No heat flux or viscosity"], "derivation": ["Rest-frame diagonal tensor is diag(epsilon,p,p,p).", "Write the unique isotropic covariant combination of u and g."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"p": 0, "u": "(c,0,0,0)"}, "steps": ["T00=epsilon c²/c².", "Spatial diagonal entries vanish."], "result": "Dust rest frame: T00=epsilon", "units": "J m^-3"}, "limitingCases": ["Radiation has p=epsilon/3, not zero"], "pitfalls": ["Anisotropic collisionless matter or magnetic stresses are not perfect fluids."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-weakmetric"><data key="title">Weak static potential in g00</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-weakmetric", "topicId": "grav-weak", "title": "Weak static potential in g00", "latex": "g_{00}\\simeq-(1+2\\Phi/c^2)", "plain": "The Newtonian potential appears in the weak static metric under a suitable gauge.", "variables": [{"symbol": "g00", "meaning": "Time-time metric component", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "Phi", "meaning": "Newtonian potential", "unit": "m² s^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["|Phi|/c² much less than1", "Static weak field and x0=ct"], "derivation": ["Expand the geodesic time-time connection.", "Match slow-particle acceleration to-gradPhi."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Phi_over_c2": -1e-06}, "steps": ["Insert into-(1+2Phi/c²).", "Keep first order only."], "result": "g00≈-0.999998", "units": "dimensionless"}, "limitingCases": ["Phi→0 gives flat time coefficient-1"], "pitfalls": ["This one component is not a complete metric for lensing or gravitational waves."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-newtonlimit"><data key="title">Newtonian limit of Einstein equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-newtonlimit", "topicId": "grav-postnewton", "title": "Newtonian limit of Einstein equation", "latex": "\\nabla^2\\Phi=4\\pi G\\rho,\\quad T_{00}\\simeq\\rho c^2", "plain": "Slow matter and weak static curvature recover the Newtonian source law.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Phi", "meaning": "Potential", "unit": "m² s^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "rho", "meaning": "Rest-mass density", "unit": "kg m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "T00", "meaning": "Energy density", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "nabla²", "meaning": "Spatial Laplacian", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Slow pressureless matter", "Weak nearly stationary field", "Compatible metric/curvature conventions"], "derivation": ["Use weakmetric and trace-reversed Einstein equation.", "Retain leading mass-density term."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"rho": 0, "boundary": "Nonzero external central mass potential"}, "steps": ["Local source density is zero.", "The harmonic exterior potential remains nonzero."], "result": "LaplacianPhi=0 outside source", "units": "s^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Strong fields require full Einstein dynamics"], "pitfalls": ["Dropping pressure is invalid for relativistic stars and early-universe radiation."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-redshift"><data key="title">Static emitted/received photon-frequency ratio</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-redshift", "topicId": "grav-redshift", "title": "Static emitted/received photon-frequency ratio", "latex": "{\\nu_B\\over\\nu_A}=\\sqrt{{-g_{00}(A)\\over-g_{00}(B)}}", "plain": "The locally measured photon frequency changes between static emitterA and receiverB. This is distinct from comparing identicallocal atomic-transition standards or their coordinate tickrates.", "variables": [{"symbol": "nuA,nuB", "meaning": "Locally emitted/received frequencies", "unit": "Hz", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "g00(A),g00(B)", "meaning": "Static time metric values", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Static metric", "Observers follow time-translation Killing flow", "No additional Doppler shift", "Matter/clockcoupling is metric and the same localtransitionstandard is used; nonmetric coupling or varyingconstants need separate modeling.", "g00(A)&lt;0 andg00(B)&lt;0: both observers follow a timelike staticKillingflow, not a horizon or ergoregion where that staticclock construction fails."], "derivation": ["Conserve photon Killing energy.", "Convert coordinate energy to local proper-time frequency."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"g00A": -0.999998, "g00B": -1}, "steps": ["Compute sqrt(0.999998).", "Expand to first order."], "result": "nuB/nuA≈0.999999", "units": "dimensionless ratio"}, "limitingCases": ["Identical potentials give unit ratio"], "pitfalls": ["Swapping emitter and receiver reverses the ratio; moving clocks require velocity terms.", "Higher static clocks accumulate moreproper time per unit staticcoordinate time, while a photon climbing outward is received redshifted. These reciprocalcomparisons must not be described with one unsignedclockshift."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-schwarzschild"><data key="title">Schwarzschild line element</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-schwarzschild", "topicId": "grav-schwarzschild", "title": "Schwarzschild line element", "latex": "ds^2=-(1-r_s/r)c^2dt^2+(1-r_s/r)^{-1}dr^2+r^2(d\\theta^2+\\sin^2\\theta\\,d\\phi^2)", "plain": "Static spherical vacuum has a horizon-coordinate singularity at r_s.", "variables": [{"symbol": "ds²", "meaning": "Interval", "unit": "m²", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r_s", "meaning": "2GM/c² length", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r", "meaning": "Areal radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "t", "meaning": "Static coordinate time", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "theta,phi", "meaning": "Polar and azimuthal angles", "unit": "rad", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Nonrotating uncharged vacuum exterior", "r&gt;r_s for static observers"], "derivation": ["Solve spherical vacuum field equations with asymptotic flatness.", "Use areal radius so spheres have area4pi r²."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"r": "10 r_s", "dr": 0, "dtheta": 0, "dphi": 0}, "steps": ["gtt factor is0.9.", "A static clock has dτ/dt=sqrt0.9."], "result": "dτ/dt≈0.948683", "units": "dimensionless ratio"}, "limitingCases": ["r≫r_s approaches flat spherical metric"], "pitfalls": ["r=r_s is not a material surface; regular coordinates cross it. Kerr requires spin terms."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-isco"><data key="title">Schwarzschild innermost stable circular orbit</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-isco", "topicId": "grav-schwarzschild", "title": "Schwarzschild innermost stable circular orbit", "latex": "r_{ISCO}=6GM/c^2=3r_s", "plain": "Marginal radial stability fixes the ISCO for test-particle timelike circular geodesics.", "variables": [{"symbol": "r_ISCO", "meaning": "Areal ISCO radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Central mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "r_s", "meaning": "Schwarzschild radius", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Nonspinning black hole", "Negligible particle self-force", "Timelike geodesic"], "derivation": ["Set first derivative of radial effective potential to zero.", "Set its second derivative to zero for marginal stability."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"M_kg": 1.98847e+30}, "steps": ["Use r_s≈2953m.", "Multiply by3."], "result": "Approximately8860m", "units": "m"}, "limitingCases": ["Kerr spin changes ISCO strongly"], "pitfalls": ["The photon orbit at3GM/c² is different from the timelike ISCO."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-precession"><data key="title">Leading periapsis advance</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-precession", "topicId": "grav-postnewton", "title": "Leading periapsis advance", "latex": "\\Delta\\varpi={6\\pi GM\\over a(1-e^2)c^2}", "plain": "Weak-field relativistic correction rotates an ideal elliptical orbit per revolution.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Delta varpi", "meaning": "Per-orbit advance", "unit": "rad", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Central mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Semimajor axis", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "e", "meaning": "Eccentricity", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Weak field", "Slow bound test orbit", "0&lt;=e&lt;1; perturbative expansion"], "derivation": ["Perturb the Schwarzschild orbit equation by3GMu²/c².", "Extract secular phase shift of radial oscillation."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_over_ac2": 1e-08, "e": 0}, "steps": ["Insert6pi×1e-8.", "Circular limit refers to nearby slightly eccentric epicycles."], "result": "1.88496e-7 rad/orbit", "units": "rad per orbit"}, "limitingCases": ["G M/(a c²)→0 gives Newton closure"], "pitfalls": ["As e→1 at fixeda, pericentre may leave the weak-field regime."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-deflection"><data key="title">Weak Schwarzschild light deflection</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-deflection", "topicId": "grav-lensing", "title": "Weak Schwarzschild light deflection", "latex": "\\alpha={4GM\\over bc^2}", "plain": "Both time and spatial metric curvature contribute to the leading asymptotic bending.", "variables": [{"symbol": "alpha", "meaning": "Bending angle", "unit": "rad", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Lens mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "b", "meaning": "Asymptotic impact parameter", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Weak deflection b≫r_s", "Source and observer far from isolated lens"], "derivation": ["Integrate the perturbed null geodesic.", "Retain first order inGM/(bc²)."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"GM_over_bc2": 1e-06}, "steps": ["Multiply by4.", "The result is small-angle radians."], "result": "4e-6rad", "units": "rad"}, "limitingCases": ["b→infinity gives zero deflection"], "pitfalls": ["Near the photon region multiple looping images require strong-field ray tracing."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-shapiro"><data key="title">Leading Shapiro delay</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-shapiro", "topicId": "grav-lensing", "title": "Leading Shapiro delay", "latex": "\\Delta t\\simeq{2GM\\over c^3}\\ln(4r_A r_B/b^2)", "plain": "A nearly conjunction ray accumulates an additional propagation delay relative to flat geometry.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Delta t", "meaning": "One-way additional delay", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Central mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "rA,rB", "meaning": "Endpoint distances to lens", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "b", "meaning": "Impact parameter", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "ln", "meaning": "Natural logarithm", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Weak static spherical field", "rA,rB≫b", "One-way convention"], "derivation": ["Integrate leading null coordinate travel time along nearly straight ray.", "Separate the geometry-dependent flat travel time."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"2GM_over_c3_s": 1e-05, "4rArB_over_b2": 100}, "steps": ["Use ln100≈4.60517.", "Multiply by1e-5s."], "result": "4.60517e-5s", "units": "s"}, "limitingCases": ["Delay vanishes with M"], "pitfalls": ["A radar round trip normally doubles a symmetric one-way result; coordinates and reference path must be specified."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-friedmann"><data key="title">First Friedmann equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-friedmann", "topicId": "grav-friedmann", "title": "First Friedmann equation", "latex": "H^2={8\\pi G\\varepsilon\\over3c^2}-{kc^2\\over a^2}+{\\Lambda c^2\\over3}", "plain": "Expansion, density, spatial curvature and Lambda obey a homogeneous-background constraint.", "variables": [{"symbol": "H", "meaning": "a dot/a Hubble rate", "unit": "s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Scale factor normalizeda0=1", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "epsilon", "meaning": "Energy density excluding explicitLambda", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "k", "meaning": "Constant spatial-curvature coefficient", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "Lambda", "meaning": "Cosmological constant", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["FLRW homogeneity/isotropy", "k has unitsm^-2 in this normalizeda convention", "ClassicalGR"], "derivation": ["Insert FLRW metric into00 Einstein component.", "Use comoving perfect-fluid stress energy."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"k": 0, "Lambda": 0, "H_s-1": 2.2683e-18}, "steps": ["Solve epsilon=3H²c²/(8piG).", "This illustrativeH is70km/s/Mpc."], "result": "epsilon≈8.27e-10J/m³", "units": "s^-2 for equation; J/m³ for example"}, "limitingCases": ["Vacuum with positiveLambda gives constantH"], "pitfalls": ["Using k=±1 while keeping a dimensionless requires a separate curvature scale; conventions must not be mixed."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-acceleration"><data key="title">FLRW acceleration equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-acceleration", "topicId": "grav-friedmann", "title": "FLRW acceleration equation", "latex": "{\\ddot a\\over a}=-{4\\pi G\\over3c^2}(\\varepsilon+3p)+{\\Lambda c^2\\over3}", "plain": "Pressure contributes to gravitational deceleration as well as energy density.", "variables": [{"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Scale factor", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "ddot a", "meaning": "Second cosmic-time derivative", "unit": "s^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "epsilon", "meaning": "Fluid energy density excludingLambda", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "p", "meaning": "Pressure", "unit": "Pa", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "Lambda", "meaning": "Explicit cosmological constant", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["FLRW perfect-fluid background", "Cosmic proper time for comoving observers"], "derivation": ["Combine spatial and temporal Einstein components.", "Use isotropy to replace stresses byp."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Lambda": 0, "p_over_epsilon": -1}, "steps": ["epsilon+3p=-2epsilon.", "The fluid contribution has positive acceleration."], "result": "ddota/a=8piG epsilon/(3c²)&gt;0", "units": "s^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Pressureless positive density decelerates withoutLambda"], "pitfalls": ["Acceleration alone does not identify a unique particle or modified-gravity mechanism."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-continuity"><data key="title">Cosmological continuity</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-continuity", "topicId": "grav-friedmann", "title": "Cosmological continuity", "latex": "\\dot\\varepsilon+3H(\\varepsilon+p)=0", "plain": "An isolated homogeneous fluid loses or gains energy density through expansion work.", "variables": [{"symbol": "epsilon", "meaning": "Energy density", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "p", "meaning": "Pressure", "unit": "Pa", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "H", "meaning": "Hubble rate", "unit": "s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "dot", "meaning": "Derivative in cosmic time", "unit": "s^-1", "kind": "operator"}], "conditions": ["Separately conserved fluid", "No inter-sector energy transfer"], "derivation": ["Use covariant stress-energy conservation.", "Equivalently apply d(epsilon a³)=-p d(a³)."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"p": 0, "a_final_over_initial": 2}, "steps": ["Integrate dust scalingepsilon∝a^-3.", "Doublinga increases volume eightfold."], "result": "Final density=initial/8", "units": "J m^-3"}, "limitingCases": ["p=-epsilon yields constant density"], "pitfalls": ["Interacting dark sectors require a source term and cannot use separate conservation unchanged."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-scaling"><data key="title">Constant equation-of-state scaling</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-scaling", "topicId": "grav-flrw", "title": "Constant equation-of-state scaling", "latex": "p=w\\varepsilon,\\quad\\varepsilon(a)=\\varepsilon_0 a^{-3(1+w)}", "plain": "A constantw closes the homogeneous continuity equation.", "variables": [{"symbol": "p", "meaning": "Pressure", "unit": "Pa", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "w", "meaning": "Constant equation-of-state ratio", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "epsilon", "meaning": "Energy density", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "epsilon0", "meaning": "Density ata=1", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Normalized scale factor", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Constantw", "Separately conserved component", "a&gt;0"], "derivation": ["Divide continuity byH epsilon.", "Integrate dln epsilon=-3(1+w)dln a."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"w": 0.3333333333333333, "a": 2, "epsilon0": 1}, "steps": ["Exponent is-4.", "Compute2^-4."], "result": "epsilon=1/16J/m³", "units": "J m^-3"}, "limitingCases": ["Dustw0 givesa^-3; vacuumw-1 givesconstant"], "pitfalls": ["A fitted time-varyingw cannot be replaced by one constant across all epochs."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-critical"><data key="title">Critical energy density</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-critical", "topicId": "grav-friedmann", "title": "Critical energy density", "latex": "\\varepsilon_c={3H^2c^2\\over8\\pi G}", "plain": "Critical energy density corresponds to flatness when all contributions are accounted consistently.", "variables": [{"symbol": "epsilon_c", "meaning": "Critical energy density", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "H", "meaning": "Hubble rate", "unit": "s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "rho_c", "meaning": "Critical mass-equivalent density epsilon_c/c²", "unit": "kg m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["FLRW background", "Do not double-countLambda as both fluid and explicit term"], "derivation": ["Set curvature contribution to zero in Friedmann.", "Solve for total effective energy density."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"H_km_s_Mpc": 70}, "steps": ["ConvertH to2.2683e-18s^-1.", "Insert constants."], "result": "epsilon_c≈8.27e-10J/m³; rho_c≈9.20e-27kg/m³", "units": "J m^-3"}, "limitingCases": ["H→0 gives zero critical density"], "pitfalls": ["Energy density epsilon_c differs byc² from mass density rho_c."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-distance"><data key="title">Flat FLRW luminosity distance</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-distance", "topicId": "grav-distances", "title": "Flat FLRW luminosity distance", "latex": "D_L(z)=(1+z)c\\int_0^z{dz^\\prime\\over H(z^\\prime)}", "plain": "Flux dilution includes both geometric distance and photon redshift/time dilation.", "variables": [{"symbol": "D_L", "meaning": "Luminosity distance", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "z,zprime", "meaning": "Cosmological redshift and integration variable", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "H", "meaning": "Expansion history", "unit": "s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Spatially flat FLRW", "Transparent metric photon propagation", "Standard luminosity-distance definition"], "derivation": ["Integrate radial null trajectory for comoving distance.", "Multiply by1+z for received flux."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"z": 0.01, "H0_s-1": 2.2683e-18}, "steps": ["At lowz useH≈H0.", "LeadingD_L≈cz/H0."], "result": "Approximately42.8Mpc at leading order", "units": "m"}, "limitingCases": ["z≪1 gives Hubble law"], "pitfalls": ["Curvature requires a transverse-distance function; luminosity and angular-diameter distance are not interchangeable."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-cpl"><data key="title">CPL equation of state</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-cpl", "topicId": "grav-cpl", "title": "CPL equation of state", "latex": "w(a)=w_0+w_a(1-a)", "plain": "Two parameters summarize a chosen time-varying dark-energy history.", "variables": [{"symbol": "w", "meaning": "p/epsilon effective ratio", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a", "meaning": "Normalized scale factor", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "w0", "meaning": "Present value", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "wa", "meaning": "Evolution parameter", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "epsilon,epsilon0", "meaning": "Dark-energy density and its presentvalue introduced in the continuityderivation", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Phenomenological parameterization", "Specified redshift range and priors"], "derivation": ["The parameterization defines w(a)=w0+wa(1-a); it is not a uniquelyderivedmicroscopic field.", "Insert into separatelyconserved fluid equation dln(epsilon)/dln(a)=-3[1+w(a)].", "Integration froma=1 gives epsilon/epsilon0=a^[-3(1+w0+wa)] exp[-3wa(1-a)], matching the densityratio inDESIDR2Eq10 after consistent mass/energy conversion."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"w0": -0.8, "wa": -0.6, "a": 0.5}, "steps": ["Compute-0.8-0.6×0.5.", "Crossingw=-1 is model-dependent."], "result": "w=-1.1", "units": "dimensionless"}, "limitingCases": ["w0=-1,wa=0 recoversLambda equation of state"], "pitfalls": ["A preference for this model is not direct detection of a new dark-energy particle.", "The analyticdensityratio does not validate the chosenw(a), establish stability, or identify the physicalcause of a distance-fit preference."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-desi-dr2", "grav-src-desi-dark"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-quadrupole"><data key="title">Far-zone quadrupole strain</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-quadrupole", "topicId": "grav-multipoles", "title": "Far-zone quadrupole strain", "latex": "h_{ij}^{TT}={2G\\over c^4D}\\ddot Q_{ij}^{TT}(t-D/c)", "plain": "Slow-source far-zone radiation is determined by a transverse trace-free mass-quadrupole projection.", "variables": [{"symbol": "hTT", "meaning": "Strain components", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "QTT", "meaning": "TT mass quadrupole", "unit": "kg m²", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "D", "meaning": "Distance", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "t", "meaning": "Observer coordinate time", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "i,j", "meaning": "Spatial indices1..3", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "dotdot", "meaning": "Second time derivative", "unit": "s^-2", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Weak far-zone radiation", "Slow source", "Distance much greater than source size/wavelength scale as appropriate"], "derivation": ["Solve linearized retarded metric equation.", "Use mass/momentum conservation to express leading radiation in quadrupole terms."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"QTT_second_kg_m2_s2": 1e+40, "D_m": 1e+20}, "steps": ["Evaluate2G Qddot/(c⁴D).", "Projection and orientation are assumed in suppliedQTT."], "result": "Approximately1.65e-24 strain", "units": "dimensionless"}, "limitingCases": ["Static quadrupole has zero second derivative and no radiation"], "pitfalls": ["Near-zone fields and relativistic merger require stronger methods."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-chirpmass"><data key="title">Binary chirp mass</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-chirpmass", "topicId": "grav-inspiral", "title": "Binary chirp mass", "latex": "\\mathcal M={(m_1m_2)^{3/5}\\over(m_1+m_2)^{1/5}}", "plain": "A mass combination controls leading inspiral phase evolution.", "variables": [{"symbol": "Mchirp", "meaning": "Source-frame chirp mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "m1,m2", "meaning": "Component source-frame masses", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Positive masses", "Leading quasi-circular inspiral"], "derivation": ["Combine reduced mass and total mass in quadrupole energy balance.", "Rewrite aseta^(3/5) totalmass."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"m1_solar": 1, "m2_solar": 1}, "steps": ["For equal massesMchirp=2^-1/5m.", "Evaluate numerical factor."], "result": "0.870551 solar masses", "units": "kg"}, "limitingCases": ["Extreme mass ratio hasMchirp much below total mass"], "pitfalls": ["Detector-frame mass is redshifted by1+z; waveform masses alone do not fix source redshift."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-chirp"><data key="title">Leading chirp-rate law</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-chirp", "topicId": "grav-inspiral", "title": "Leading chirp-rate law", "latex": "\\dot f={96\\over5}\\pi^{8/3}\\left({G\\mathcal M\\over c^3}\\right)^{5/3}f^{11/3}", "plain": "Gravitational-wave frequency rises as a quasi-circular binary loses orbital energy.", "variables": [{"symbol": "fdot", "meaning": "GW frequency derivative", "unit": "Hz s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "f", "meaning": "GW frequency twice orbital frequency", "unit": "Hz", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "Mchirp", "meaning": "Detector-frame chirp mass for observedf", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Leading quadrupole order", "Quasi-circular adiabatic inspiral", "Not merger"], "derivation": ["Differentiate Newtonian orbital energy with frequency.", "Equate its loss to quadrupole radiated power."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Mchirp_kg": 1.98847e+30, "f_Hz": 100}, "steps": ["InsertSI constants andf.", "Use detector-frame mass with observedtime."], "result": "Approximately12.49Hz/s", "units": "Hz s^-1"}, "limitingCases": ["Smallf strongly suppresses chirp"], "pitfalls": ["Spins, eccentricity and post-Newtonian effects alter the waveform; do not extrapolate through merger."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-amplitude"><data key="title">Leading circular-binary amplitude scale</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-amplitude", "topicId": "grav-inspiral", "title": "Leading circular-binary amplitude scale", "latex": "h_0={4(G\\mathcal M)^{5/3}(\\pi f)^{2/3}\\over c^4D}", "plain": "An amplitude scale depends on distance and mass as well as frequency.", "variables": [{"symbol": "h0", "meaning": "Orientation-unprojected leading strain scale", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "Mchirp", "meaning": "Chirp mass consistent with frequency frame", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "f", "meaning": "GW frequency", "unit": "Hz", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "D", "meaning": "Appropriate luminosity distance", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Leading circular inspiral", "Polarization/inclination factors applied separately", "Cosmological redshift convention consistent"], "derivation": ["Insert circular orbit quadrupole into far-zone formula.", "Use Kepler relation to remove orbital separation."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"Mchirp_kg": 1.98847e+30, "f_Hz": 100, "D_Mpc": 100}, "steps": ["Convert100Mpc to metres.", "Evaluate leading scale only."], "result": "Approximately2.6e-23", "units": "dimensionless"}, "limitingCases": ["Doubling distance halves amplitude"], "pitfalls": ["Inclination-distance degeneracy prevents unique distance from one scalar amplitude."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-ringdown"><data key="title">Damped ringdown component</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-ringdown", "topicId": "grav-qnm", "title": "Damped ringdown component", "latex": "h(t)=A e^{-t/\\tau}\\cos(2\\pi f_Rt+\\varphi)", "plain": "A selected quasinormal contribution has a decay time and oscillation frequency.", "variables": [{"symbol": "h", "meaning": "Strain contribution", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "A", "meaning": "Initial amplitude", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "t", "meaning": "Time since chosen start", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "tau", "meaning": "Positive damping time", "unit": "s", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "fR", "meaning": "Real oscillation frequency", "unit": "Hz", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "varphi", "meaning": "Phase", "unit": "rad", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "omega", "meaning": "Complex angular frequency in exp(-i omega t) convention", "unit": "rad s^-1", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "i", "meaning": "Imaginary unit, i²=-1", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Linear black-hole perturbation after a justified start", "One selected mode", "No growing instability assumed"], "derivation": ["Use complexfrequencyomega=2pi fR-i/tau withexp(-iomega t).", "Take a real component with adjusted phase."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"A": 1, "t_over_tau": 1, "phase": "at cosine maximum"}, "steps": ["The envelope is exp(-1).", "Mode interference is omitted."], "result": "Envelope≈0.367879", "units": "dimensionless"}, "limitingCases": ["tau→infinity removes damping"], "pitfalls": ["A short fitted damped sinusoid alone does not establish a Kerr spectrum or unique mode identification."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-carroll"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-hd"><data key="title">Hellings–Downs angular curve</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-hd", "topicId": "grav-hd", "title": "Hellings–Downs angular curve", "latex": "\\zeta_{ab}={3\\over2}x\\ln x-{x\\over4}+{1\\over2}+{1\\over2}\\delta_{ab},\\quad x={1-\\cos\\theta_{ab}\\over2}", "plain": "The ideal isotropic tensor-background correlation has a distinctive angular shape.", "variables": [{"symbol": "zeta", "meaning": "Normalized timing correlation", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "theta_ab", "meaning": "Pulsar angular separation", "unit": "rad", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "x", "meaning": "Angular helper", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "delta_ab", "meaning": "1 for samepulsar else0", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "a,b", "meaning": "Pulsar labels", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["GR transverse tensor polarizations", "Isotropic unpolarized stochastic background", "Standard pulsar-term averaging and normalization"], "derivation": ["Average products of pulsar antenna responses over sky directions.", "Retain autocorrelation normalization separately."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"theta_rad": 3.141592653589793, "a_equals_b": false}, "steps": ["Thenx=1 andln1=0.", "Compute-1/4+1/2."], "result": "zeta=1/4", "units": "dimensionless"}, "limitingCases": ["For distinct co-aligned pulsars xlnx→0 andzeta→1/2"], "pitfalls": ["Spatially common red noise without the correlation pattern is not equivalent evidence for this model."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-pta"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-semiclassical"><data key="title">Semiclassical Einstein equation</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">approximation</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-semiclassical", "topicId": "grav-semiclassical", "title": "Semiclassical Einstein equation", "latex": "G_{\\mu\\nu}+\\Lambda g_{\\mu\\nu}={8\\pi G\\over c^4}\\langle\\hat T_{\\mu\\nu}\\rangle_{ren}", "plain": "A classical metric is sourced by a renormalized quantum stress expectation in a chosen state.", "variables": [{"symbol": "G_munu", "meaning": "Einstein tensor", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "Lambda", "meaning": "Cosmological constant", "unit": "m^-2", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "g_munu", "meaning": "Metric", "unit": "dimensionless in length chart", "kind": "tensor"}, {"symbol": "T_hat", "meaning": "Quantum stress operator", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "operator"}, {"symbol": "expectation", "meaning": "State-dependent renormalized mean", "unit": "J m^-3", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "mu,nu", "meaning": "Spacetime indices", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["Specified quantum state and renormalization prescription", "Controlled stress fluctuations", "Not asserted fundamental at all scales"], "derivation": ["Vary a suitable renormalized effective action or use mean-field approximation.", "Include necessary gravitational counterterms when required."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"state": "Renormalized Minkowski vacuum", "Lambda": 0}, "steps": ["Set the reference vacuum stress to zero consistently.", "Flat metric is then a conditional solution."], "result": "0=0 under stated renormalization conditions", "units": "m^-2"}, "limitingCases": ["Large stress fluctuations can invalidate a mean-source approximation"], "pitfalls": ["It is not a complete theory of quantum metric fluctuations."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-eft"], "status": "approximation", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-planck"><data key="title">Planck length</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">established-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-planck", "topicId": "grav-planck", "title": "Planck length", "latex": "\\ell_P=\\sqrt{\\hbar G/c^3}", "plain": "A dimensional length combines quantum action, gravity and relativity.", "variables": [{"symbol": "ellP", "meaning": "Planck length", "unit": "m", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "hbar", "meaning": "Reduced Planck constant", "unit": "J s", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}], "conditions": ["SI constants", "Dimensional scale, not a derived universal minimum distance"], "derivation": ["Require a length monomial inħ,G,c.", "Solve dimensions for exponents1/2,1/2,-3/2."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"G_SI": 6.6743e-11}, "steps": ["Useħ=1.054571817e-34J s andc=299792458m/s.", "Evaluate square root."], "result": "Approximately1.61626e-35m", "units": "m"}, "limitingCases": ["G→0 makes this gravity-dependent scale vanish"], "pitfalls": ["Dimensional analysis does not establish measured area discreteness or a UV completion."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-eft", "grav-src-codata"], "status": "established-model", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-f-hawking"><data key="title">Schwarzschild Hawking temperature</data><data key="kind">formula</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">conditional-result</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-f-hawking", "topicId": "grav-hawking", "title": "Schwarzschild Hawking temperature", "latex": "T_H={\\hbar c^3\\over8\\pi G M k_B}", "plain": "A nonrotating black hole has a semiclassical temperature defined relative to asymptotic time.", "variables": [{"symbol": "TH", "meaning": "Hawking temperature", "unit": "K", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "M", "meaning": "Black-hole mass", "unit": "kg", "kind": "scalar"}, {"symbol": "hbar", "meaning": "Reduced Planck constant", "unit": "J s", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "c", "meaning": "Vacuum light speed", "unit": "m s^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "pi", "meaning": "Circle constant", "unit": "dimensionless", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "G", "meaning": "Newtonian gravitational constant", "unit": "m^3 kg^-1 s^-2", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "k_B", "meaning": "Boltzmann constant", "unit": "J K^-1", "kind": "constant"}, {"symbol": "kappa", "meaning": "Surface gravity with asymptotic time normalization", "unit": "m s^-2", "kind": "scalar"}], "conditions": ["Quantum fields on a semiclassical Schwarzschild background", "Large enough mass for small curvature at horizon", "Asymptotic normalization"], "derivation": ["Relate horizon surfacegravity to thermal periodicity or Bogoliubov particle creation.", "Useκ=c⁴/(4GM) andkBT=ħκ/(2pi c)."], "workedExample": {"inputs": {"M_kg": 1.98847e+30}, "steps": ["Insert solar mass.", "The predicted temperature is extremely low."], "result": "Approximately6.17e-8K", "units": "K"}, "limitingCases": ["LargerM gives lowerTH"], "pitfalls": ["This is not a direct detection of Hawking radiation from an astrophysical black hole."], "sourceIds": ["grav-src-hawking"], "status": "conditional-result", "kind": "formula", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-carroll"><data key="title">Lecture Notes on General Relativity</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-carroll", "title": "Lecture Notes on General Relativity", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9712019", "authors": ["Carroll, Sean M."], "year": 1997, "version": "1997/12/03; 1997/12/03", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "readDepth": "Selected text: lecture introduction and metric/connection/curvature/Einstein/Schwarzschild/cosmology formula passages", "sectionsRead": ["Selected text: lecture introduction and metric/connection/curvature/Einstein/Schwarzschild/cosmology formula passages"], "claim": "Geometry, waves and cosmology are presented in one declared GR framework.", "limitations": "Pedagogical notes, not an experimental dataset; not every page read.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Geometry, waves and cosmology are presented in one declared GR framework.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-carroll-pdf.pdf", "sha256": "d4cbfeed3a18370cb7e1a256da6fa7de722982ad7f6a146b4fc0fe14a6bebf6c", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:25:59.363598+00:00", "doi": null, "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "textbook", "sourceKind": "textbook"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-desi-dr2"><data key="title">DESI DR2 Results II: Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations and Cosmological Constraints</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-desi-dr2", "title": "DESI DR2 Results II: Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations and Cosmological Constraints", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14738v3", "authors": ["DESI Collaboration", "Abdul-Karim, M.", "Aguilar, J.", "Ahlen, S.", "Alam, S.", "Allen, L."], "year": 2025, "version": "arXiv2503.14738v3,9October2025; complete12,175,089-bytePDF captured2026-11-25", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "readDepth": "Complete PDF downloaded and text extracted; selected model/equation, §II data, BAO/covariance/TableIII–IV context, model-comparison/TableVI passage and §IX conclusions read. Remainingappendices and likelihood/data not independently reanalysed.", "sectionsRead": ["Model definitions and Eq10 dark-energy density evolution", "§II DESIData; tracer/selection/pipeline context", "BAOmeasurements and TableIII–IV covariance/composite-tracer cautions", "Evolvingdarkenergy model-comparison/TableVI and SNcompilation dependence", "§IX Conclusions"], "claim": "BAOalone is well described by flatLambdaCDM in the source. Combining DESIBAO withCMB and supernova compilations changes the evolving-w model preference; Pantheon+/Union3/DESY5 combinations report2.8/3.8/4.2sigma in the inspectedversion.", "limitations": "Source-reported/model-conditional inference, not replicatedlikelihoods or direct identification of a dark-energyfield. DR1is contained inDR2, correlatedtracers are not independent datasets, and equation-of-state history is indirectlyinferred. Original8MBattempt was truncated; thisR2capture replaces it as selected-text evidence.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Selected primary-text review; modelparameterization, combineddatasetchoice, blindedpipeline validation and uncertainty treatment qualify the reported preference.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-r2-desi-dr2.pdf", "sha256": "1e82f26e4cc3901b16168cd147f252bfa804f9c3caad3f4f7e3532640d237841", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:44:07.345615+00:00", "doi": "10.1103/tr6y-kpc6", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-desi-dark"><data key="title">Extended Dark Energy analysis using DESI DR2 BAO measurements</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-desi-dark", "title": "Extended Dark Energy analysis using DESI DR2 BAO measurements", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14743", "authors": ["Lodha, K.", "Calderon, R.", "Matthewson, W. L.", "Shafieloo, A.", "Ishak, M.", "Pan, J."], "year": 2025, "version": "2025/03/18; 2025/04/03", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "readDepth": "Abstract and selected PDF introduction/conclusions/model-comparison passages", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and selected PDF introduction/conclusions/model-comparison passages"], "claim": "Parametric and nonparametric extensions explore robustness of inferred evolving-dark-energy trends.", "limitations": "An abstract/selected passage reading is not a reanalysis of likelihoods or a validation of all systematic choices.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Parametric and nonparametric extensions explore robustness of inferred evolving-dark-energy trends.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-desi-dark-pdf.pdf", "sha256": "0de007414e3464ca00c81950a1db42c6be4a15dcac9bbabc559a7656e094274d", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:25:59.364830+00:00", "doi": null, "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "preprint", "sourceKind": "preprint"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-desi-dr1"><data key="title">DESI 2024 VI: Cosmological Constraints from the Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-desi-dr1", "title": "DESI 2024 VI: Cosmological Constraints from the Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.03002", "authors": ["DESI Collaboration", "Adame, A. G.", "Aguilar, J.", "Ahlen, S.", "Alam, S.", "Alexander, D. M."], "year": 2024, "version": "2024/04/03; 2024/11/04", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The first-yearDESI BAO analysis constrains distance ratios. Author-reported evolving-dark-energy preferences vary with the CMB and supernova combination.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The first-yearDESI BAO analysis constrains distance ratios. Author-reported evolving-dark-energy preferences vary with the CMB and supernova combination.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-desi-dr1.html", "sha256": "a6eaf578b420ad4571eb5dad1de39e08c395f8b1627eb74604cb9318470b734c", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.479962+00:00", "doi": "10.1088/1475-7516/2025/02/021", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-pta"><data key="title">The NANOGrav 15-year Data Set: Evidence for a Gravitational-Wave Background</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-pta", "title": "The NANOGrav 15-year Data Set: Evidence for a Gravitational-Wave Background", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.16213", "authors": ["Agazie, Gabriella", "Anumarlapudi, Akash", "Archibald, Anne M.", "Arzoumanian, Zaven", "Baker, Paul T.", "Becsy, Bence"], "year": 2023, "version": "2023/06/28; 2023/06/28", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The15-yearNANOGrav abstract reports angular timing correlations consistent with a Hellings–Downs tensor background. Spectral/model choices affect reported evidence and do not uniquely identify origin.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The15-yearNANOGrav abstract reports angular timing correlations consistent with a Hellings–Downs tensor background. Spectral/model choices affect reported evidence and do not uniquely identify origin.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-pta.html", "sha256": "4173ca8d574b2b4dd10d2eee9847c39f69d6616bc7d47119dee13c833da8ae20", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.480581+00:00", "doi": "10.3847/2041-8213/acdac6", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-gwtc-tests"><data key="title">Tests of General Relativity with GWTC-3</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-gwtc-tests", "title": "Tests of General Relativity with GWTC-3", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.06861", "authors": ["The LIGO Scientific Collaboration", "the Virgo Collaboration", "the KAGRA Collaboration", "Abbott, R.", "Abe, H.", "Acernese, F."], "year": 2021, "version": "2021/12/13; 2025/11/17", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The selectedGWTC-3 abstract reports consistency withGR in residual,dispersion,polarization and remnant tests under its event/waveform assumptions.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The selectedGWTC-3 abstract reports consistency withGR in residual,dispersion,polarization and remnant tests under its event/waveform assumptions.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-gwtc-tests.html", "sha256": "cf13e4d66799f3e31552e408727b5b71a3f96740f5056b75866ae276f8a87219", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.480920+00:00", "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevD.112.084080", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-microscope"><data key="title">MICROSCOPE mission: final results of the test of the Equivalence Principle</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-microscope", "title": "MICROSCOPE mission: final results of the test of the Equivalence Principle", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.15487", "authors": ["Touboul, Pierre", "Métris, Gilles", "Rodrigues, Manuel", "Bergé, Joel", "Robert, Alain", "Baghi, Quentin"], "year": 2022, "version": "2022/09/30; 2022/09/30", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The mission compares titanium/platinum free fall and reports no composition-dependent violation within statistical and systematic uncertainties at its tested sensitivity.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The mission compares titanium/platinum free fall and reports no composition-dependent violation within statistical and systematic uncertainties at its tested sensitivity.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-microscope.html", "sha256": "4a60abd700a2d34693506405f538d47bba74c0ec5ed9c8425d788ac87baf8e35", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.481791+00:00", "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.129.121102", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-q-entangle"><data key="title">A Spin Entanglement Witness for Quantum Gravity</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-q-entangle", "title": "A Spin Entanglement Witness for Quantum Gravity", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.06050", "authors": ["Bose, Sougato", "Mazumdar, Anupam", "Morley, Gavin W.", "Ulbricht, Hendrik", "Toroš, Marko", "Paternostro, Mauro"], "year": 2017, "version": "2017/07/19; 2017/07/19", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The authors propose entangling separated masses through a gravitational interaction and witnessing spin correlations under stated mediation assumptions. This is not a performedexperiment.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The authors propose entangling separated masses through a gravitational interaction and witnessing spin correlations under stated mediation assumptions. This is not a performedexperiment.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-q-entangle.html", "sha256": "41700e19f81d32221c6f6d3562d6eec387b49aa3c9248e91f93e1f15a13554fe", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.750731+00:00", "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.240401", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-eft"><data key="title">General relativity as an effective field theory: The leading quantum corrections</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-eft", "title": "General relativity as an effective field theory: The leading quantum corrections", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9405057", "authors": ["Donoghue, John F."], "year": 1994, "version": "1994/05/25; 1994/05/25", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The author develops low-energy effectivegravity, separating calculable long-distance quantum contributions from unknown high-energy effects.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The author develops low-energy effectivegravity, separating calculable long-distance quantum contributions from unknown high-energy effects.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-eft.html", "sha256": "f1afa9a22d8a8eec01dfaca5b8628e4310845fd42b7f5c8b12e39b2b35ea232b", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.760746+00:00", "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevD.50.3874", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-ads"><data key="title">The Large N Limit of Superconformal Field Theories and Supergravity</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-ads", "title": "The Large N Limit of Superconformal Field Theories and Supergravity", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711200", "authors": ["Maldacena, Juan M."], "year": 1997, "version": "1997/11/27; 1998/01/22", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The abstract identifies controlled large-N/near-horizon relationships and conjectures broaderAdS/string–field-theory dualities under specified conditions.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The abstract identifies controlled large-N/near-horizon relationships and conjectures broaderAdS/string–field-theory dualities under specified conditions.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-ads.html", "sha256": "3758aa063f3b3f0d1240b3989a3827d971ad2000fa243989eab5d0a2641647e5", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.771381+00:00", "doi": "10.1023/A:1026654312961", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-lqg"><data key="title">Discreteness of area and volume in quantum gravity</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-lqg", "title": "Discreteness of area and volume in quantum gravity", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9411005", "authors": ["Rovelli, Carlo", "Smolin, Lee"], "year": 1994, "version": "1994/11/02; 1994/11/02", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only", "sectionsRead": ["Abstract and bibliographic/version metadata only"], "claim": "The authors construct geometricoperators in a looprepresentation and describe discrete spectra. This does not establish measuredspacetime discreteness or complete physicaldynamics.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The authors construct geometricoperators in a looprepresentation and describe discrete spectra. This does not establish measuredspacetime discreteness or complete physicaldynamics.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-lqg.html", "sha256": "855ffa238e9973188107ef0e67ca1cfd6872e0db5dbbfae35a805e6c5ab23280", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.823197+00:00", "doi": "10.1016/0550-3213(95)00150-Q", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-gwosc"><data key="title">GWOSC all-events catalogue index, captured2026-11-25</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">metadata-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-gwosc", "title": "GWOSC all-events catalogue index, captured2026-11-25", "url": "https://gwosc.org/eventapi/json/allevents/", "authors": ["LIGO/Virgo/KAGRA / GWOSC"], "year": null, "version": "Dated APIcapture; catalogue labels are metadata, not a guarantee of continuouslylatestrelease", "kind": "source", "status": "metadata-only", "readDepth": "OfficialAPI top-level events structure and catalogue labels inspected; no strainwaveforms reanalysed. EarlierGWTC3selection-page reading preserved inR1freeze.", "sectionsRead": ["events catalog.shortName metadata labels", "Selected event record metadata structure"], "claim": "The retrievedofficialindex contains GWTC-4.0,GWTC-4.1 andGWTC-5.0 labels alongside oldercatalogues. This atlas therefore treats its olderGWTC3test paper as a historicalselectedbaseline, not the latestcatalogue.", "limitations": "An event-index capture is not a fullcataloguepaper review, detectorcalibration audit or independentlycleanedstrain dataset. Do not infer unreadeventproperties or comprehensivecurrentliterature from labels.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Official data-index metadata anchors cataloguechronology and source-access context; analysis claims rely on separatelyreadprimarypapers.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-r2-gwosc-catalogues.json", "sha256": "731f167b5545db5b3b4345994fde52730e260bb1112a739051be7f884fca7969", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:44:07.346707+00:00", "doi": null, "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "official-data", "sourceKind": "official-data"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-codata"><data key="title">2022CODATA Newtonian constant of gravitation</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-codata", "title": "2022CODATA Newtonian constant of gravitation", "url": "https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?bg", "authors": ["NIST/CODATA"], "year": 2022, "version": "Captured2026-11-25; source-specific edition noted", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "readDepth": "NumericalG,standarduncertainty,units and2022CODATA attribution", "sectionsRead": ["NumericalG,standarduncertainty,units and2022CODATA attribution"], "claim": "G=6.67430(15)e-11m³kg^-1s^-2 is measured with relative standard uncertainty2.2e-5.", "limitations": "Not an exact defined constant; a quoted standard uncertainty is not a universal confidence interval.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "G=6.67430(15)e-11m³kg^-1s^-2 is measured with relative standard uncertainty2.2e-5.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-src-codata.html", "sha256": "c8ce82543b405f67d2afb2fb4782abd487cd474d50942c85b9f03b408b113510", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:23:57.883702+00:00", "doi": null, "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "official-data", "sourceKind": "official-data"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-pdg"><data key="title">Experimental Tests of Gravitational Theory, PDG2025</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-pdg", "title": "Experimental Tests of Gravitational Theory, PDG2025", "url": "https://pdg.lbl.gov/2025/reviews/rpp2025-rev-gravity-tests.pdf", "authors": ["T.Damour / ParticleDataGroup"], "year": 2025, "version": "Captured2026-11-25; source-specific edition noted", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "re