0c7d4e50492", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:25:59.365277+00:00", "doi": null, "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "primary-paper", "sourceKind": "primary-paper"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-2026-1"><data key="title">Gravity-mediated entanglement via infinite-dimensional systems</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">metadata-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-2026-1", "title": "Gravity-mediated entanglement via infinite-dimensional systems", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8121/ae65e7", "authors": ["Stefan L Ludescher", "Leon D Loveridge", "Thomas D Galley", "Markus P Müller"], "year": 2026, "version": "Crossref publisher-deposited date[2026, 5, 27]", "kind": "source", "status": "metadata-only", "readDepth": "Exact-title/DOI/date discovery metadata only; publisher full article not accessible", "sectionsRead": ["Bibliographic metadata only"], "claim": "A2026theory record exists concerning gravity-related entanglement; no result from unread text admitted.", "limitations": "IOP200response was an error page; guessedAPSjournal route404. Metadata is not article reading or experimental evidence.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Unreviewed2026lead retained to expose the cutoff/search gap, not to certify novelty.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/discovery-gravity-2026.json", "sha256": "3b69da6fb7b8df362255686f927aff4edacb6d6a39c2ec293e08a92b49f696eb", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:33:43.798846+00:00", "doi": "10.1088/1751-8121/ae65e7", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "metadata", "sourceKind": "metadata"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-2026-2"><data key="title">Matter-mediated entanglement by classical gravity under realistic matter dynamics</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">metadata-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-2026-2", "title": "Matter-mediated entanglement by classical gravity under realistic matter dynamics", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1103/bg9v-ln16", "authors": ["Ziqian Tang", "Chen Yang", "Hanyu Xue", "Haochen Yu", "Zizhao Han", "Zikuan Kan", "Yulong Liu"], "year": 2026, "version": "Crossref publisher-deposited date[2026, 11, 20]", "kind": "source", "status": "metadata-only", "readDepth": "Exact-title/DOI/date discovery metadata only; publisher full article not accessible", "sectionsRead": ["Bibliographic metadata only"], "claim": "A2026theory record exists concerning gravity-related entanglement; no result from unread text admitted.", "limitations": "IOP200response was an error page; guessedAPSjournal route404. Metadata is not article reading or experimental evidence.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Unreviewed2026lead retained to expose the cutoff/search gap, not to certify novelty.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/discovery-gravity-2026.json", "sha256": "3b69da6fb7b8df362255686f927aff4edacb6d6a39c2ec293e08a92b49f696eb", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:33:43.798846+00:00", "doi": "10.1103/bg9v-ln16", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "metadata", "sourceKind": "metadata"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-eht-record"><data key="title">The persistent shadow of the supermassive black hole of M87</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">metadata-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-eht-record", "title": "The persistent shadow of the supermassive black hole of M87", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202451296", "authors": "Event Horizon Telescope Collaboration; complete attribution in linked source", "year": 2025, "version": "Crossref date2025-01", "kind": "source", "status": "metadata-only", "readDepth": "Title,DOI,publicationdate and publisherPDFlink metadata; PDFaccess403", "sectionsRead": ["Bibliographic metadata only"], "claim": "A2025M87persistent-shadow paper is indexed; this chapter does not claim its full analysis was read.", "limitations": "Initial guessedarXiv2401.12709 was unrelatedviscoelasticity and rejected. EHTbrightness imaging requires emission/calibration priors; no new EHTnumeric result imported.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "Source identity is mapped; detailed paper review remains an explicit gap.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/discovery-eht.json", "sha256": "b4ef205266539d9c9298c6313f2daa984163cd78b4b19dda549fe1f9bac879ba", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:33:43.798846+00:00", "doi": "10.1051/0004-6361/202451296", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "metadata", "sourceKind": "metadata"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-gwtc5"><data key="title">GWTC-5.0: Tests of General Relativity</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-gwtc5", "title": "GWTC-5.0: Tests of General Relativity", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.19293v1", "authors": ["The LIGO Scientific Collaboration", "the Virgo Collaboration", "the KAGRA Collaboration", "Abac, A. G."], "year": 2026, "version": "arXiv2607.19293v1;firstposted2026/07/21", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "passageKind": "research-note", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-r2-gwtc5-paper.pdf", "sha256": "4ab5df879daa2f4acd2d9fac32e64f5daf78d8fddd73ba5d76ecc5a2047ab101", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:45:55.434193+00:00", "readDepth": "Complete PDF downloaded/extracted; title/abstract, eventselection and omitted-test/systematic passages, selected waveform/QNM Eq19–20 passage, and §8 conclusions read. Data,fulltables andcode not independentlyreanalysed.", "sectionsRead": ["Title/abstract anddatedv1header", "Selection:two-detector andFAR threshold;new/cumulative eventcounts", "Explicit omittedtests and knownbias/scope limitations", "Selected QNM/complexfrequency and waveformmatching passage Eq19–20", "§8 Conclusions"], "claim": "The2026preprint reports seven selectedGRtests using a cumulative168events under itsselection. It reports no significantbeyond-GR evidence in those tests, while explicitlydiscussing finitecatalogue effects and ringdownsystematics.", "limitations": "A selectedpreprint, not an exhaustiveNov2026survey or proof ofGR. Some tests are omitted becauseof knownbiases,weakconstraints orscope. Combinedringdown results include edge-of-credible-region behavior andfinite-sample uncertainty; an overtone can be contaminated by unmodeledcontent.", "note": "The source improves chronologicalcoverage beyondGWTC3 while making testselection,calibration,baselinewaveforms andomittedtests visible.", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "preprint", "sourceKind": "preprint"}</data></node><node id="grav-src-gw250114"><data key="title">Black Hole Spectroscopy and Tests of General Relativity with GW250114</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-src-gw250114", "title": "Black Hole Spectroscopy and Tests of General Relativity with GW250114", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.08099v1", "authors": ["The LIGO Scientific Collaboration", "the Virgo Collaboration", "the KAGRA Collaboration"], "year": 2025, "version": "arXiv2509.08099v1;firstposted2025/09/09", "kind": "source", "status": "selected-text", "passageKind": "research-note", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/gravity/grav-r2-gw250114-paper.pdf", "sha256": "8514216587c4a21797b6ebe69643712395daf280a3646542cbe8b8824892f809", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:45:55.435050+00:00", "readDepth": "Complete PDF downloaded/extracted; title/abstract, eventmodel assumptions, BHspectroscopy method, full-signal/pSEOBNR Fig4 passage and440mode-presence caveat read. Supplementaryanalyses andrawdata not reanalysed.", "sectionsRead": ["Title/abstract andv1date", "GW250114 eventmodel andremnant spectroscopy definitions", "QNM model,starttime anddamping context", "Full-signal pSEOBNR/Fig4 constraints and explicit440presence caveat"], "claim": "The selected2025preprint reports tests ofGW250114 using ringdown andfull-signal models. It explicitly says its440frequencyconstraint cannot byitself establish that the440mode is present because themodel enforces waveformcontinuity/nonzeroamplitudes.", "limitations": "Source-era single-eventclaims,not a continuouslylatestloudestevent assertion. Modepresence,deviationparameters,starttime andwaveformassumptions are distinct. Noindependent detector-data analysis,noise/calibration audit ormode-detection replication here.", "note": "A concrete counterexample to equating a fittedspectralfrequencybound with a free-standing detection of thatmode; physical interpretation depends on thelikelihood/model.", "domain": "gravity", "recordKind": "preprint", "sourceKind": "preprint"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-desi-dr2"><data key="title">DESI DR2 Results II: Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations and Cosmological Constraints</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-desi-dr2", "sourceId": "grav-src-desi-dr2", "topicIds": ["grav-desi"], "question": "Do DR2distance measurements prefer a constant dark-energy equation of state?", "method": "BAOdistances combined withCMB and alternativeSNcompilations.", "result": "BAOalone is well described by flatLambdaCDM in the source. Combining DESIBAO withCMB and supernova compilations changes the evolving-w model preference; Pantheon+/Union3/DESY5 combinations report2.8/3.8/4.2sigma in the inspectedversion.", "whatIsNew": "Three-yearDESIdistance information sharpens model comparisons.", "limitations": "Source-reported/model-conditional inference, not replicatedlikelihoods or direct identification of a dark-energyfield. DR1is contained inDR2, correlatedtracers are not independent datasets, and equation-of-state history is indirectlyinferred. Original8MBattempt was truncated; thisR2capture replaces it as selected-text evidence.", "status": "selected-text; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "DESI DR2 Results II: Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations and Cosmological Constraints", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-desi-dark"><data key="title">Extended Dark Energy analysis using DESI DR2 BAO measurements</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-desi-dark", "sourceId": "grav-src-desi-dark", "topicIds": ["grav-cpl"], "question": "How stable are inferred dark-energy trends to parameterization?", "method": "Parametric plus nonparametric reconstructions and model-class comparisons.", "result": "Parametric and nonparametric extensions explore robustness of inferred evolving-dark-energy trends.", "whatIsNew": "Extended methods probe the same data rather than providing independent observations.", "limitations": "An abstract/selected passage reading is not a reanalysis of likelihoods or a validation of all systematic choices.", "status": "selected-text; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": ["grav-f-cpl"], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "Extended Dark Energy analysis using DESI DR2 BAO measurements", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-desi-dr1"><data key="title">DESI 2024 VI: Cosmological Constraints from the Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-desi-dr1", "sourceId": "grav-src-desi-dr1", "topicIds": ["grav-desi"], "question": "What did first-yearBAOconstrain?", "method": "Galaxy/quasar/forest clustering and combined cosmological likelihoods.", "result": "The first-yearDESI BAO analysis constrains distance ratios. Author-reported evolving-dark-energy preferences vary with the CMB and supernova combination.", "whatIsNew": "A source-reported first-yearbaseline for laterDR2comparison.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "DESI 2024 VI: Cosmological Constraints from the Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-pta"><data key="title">The NANOGrav 15-year Data Set: Evidence for a Gravitational-Wave Background</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-pta", "sourceId": "grav-src-pta", "topicIds": ["grav-hd"], "question": "Are pulsar residual correlations consistent with a tensor background?", "method": "Correlated-red-noise Bayesian and frequentist comparisons.", "result": "The15-yearNANOGrav abstract reports angular timing correlations consistent with a Hellings–Downs tensor background. Spectral/model choices affect reported evidence and do not uniquely identify origin.", "whatIsNew": "Angular correlation evidence beyond an uncorrelatedcommonprocess.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": ["grav-f-hd"], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "The NANOGrav 15-year Data Set: Evidence for a Gravitational-Wave Background", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-gwtc-tests"><data key="title">Tests of General Relativity with GWTC-3</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-gwtc-tests", "sourceId": "grav-src-gwtc-tests", "topicIds": ["grav-qnm"], "question": "Are compact-binary waveforms consistent with selectedGRtests?", "method": "Residual,inspiral,polarization,dispersion and remnant consistency tests.", "result": "The selectedGWTC-3 abstract reports consistency withGR in residual,dispersion,polarization and remnant tests under its event/waveform assumptions.", "whatIsNew": "A selectedcatalogue test suite; not universal proof ofGR.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": ["grav-f-ringdown"], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "Tests of General Relativity with GWTC-3", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-microscope"><data key="title">MICROSCOPE mission: final results of the test of the Equivalence Principle</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-microscope", "sourceId": "grav-src-microscope", "topicIds": ["grav-microscope"], "question": "Does composition change free-fall acceleration?", "method": "Differential electrostatic accelerometers and systematic-error characterization.", "result": "The mission compares titanium/platinum free fall and reports no composition-dependent violation within statistical and systematic uncertainties at its tested sensitivity.", "whatIsNew": "Titanium/platinum differential constraint at mission sensitivity.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "MICROSCOPE mission: final results of the test of the Equivalence Principle", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-q-entangle"><data key="title">A Spin Entanglement Witness for Quantum Gravity</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-q-entangle", "sourceId": "grav-src-q-entangle", "topicIds": ["grav-witness"], "question": "Can a gravitational interaction create a measurable entanglement witness?", "method": "Proposed separatedmassinterferometers andspinreadout.", "result": "The authors propose entangling separated masses through a gravitational interaction and witnessing spin correlations under stated mediation assumptions. This is not a performedexperiment.", "whatIsNew": "A conditionalexperimentalproposal, not a performed gravity-entanglement experiment.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "A Spin Entanglement Witness for Quantum Gravity", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-eft"><data key="title">General relativity as an effective field theory: The leading quantum corrections</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-eft", "sourceId": "grav-src-eft", "topicIds": ["grav-eft"], "question": "Can low-energy quantumgravity be predictive withoutUVcompletion?", "method": "Effective-field-theory separation of long-distance terms and matched localcoefficients.", "result": "The author develops low-energy effectivegravity, separating calculable long-distance quantum contributions from unknown high-energy effects.", "whatIsNew": "A controlledlowenergyframework under its assumptions.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "General relativity as an effective field theory: The leading quantum corrections", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-ads"><data key="title">The Large N Limit of Superconformal Field Theories and Supergravity</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-ads", "sourceId": "grav-src-ads", "topicIds": ["grav-ads"], "question": "Which large-Nfieldtheories encode selectedAdSgravityregimes?", "method": "Branedecoupling andnearhorizonlargeNarguments.", "result": "The abstract identifies controlled large-N/near-horizon relationships and conjectures broaderAdS/string–field-theory dualities under specified conditions.", "whatIsNew": "An influentialdualityproposal under specificsymmetry/boundaryconditions.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "The Large N Limit of Superconformal Field Theories and Supergravity", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-lqg"><data key="title">Discreteness of area and volume in quantum gravity</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-lqg", "sourceId": "grav-src-lqg", "topicIds": ["grav-area"], "question": "What spectra arise for geometricoperators in a looprepresentation?", "method": "Regularizedarea/volumeoperators andspinnetworkstates.", "result": "The authors construct geometricoperators in a looprepresentation and describe discrete spectra. This does not establish measuredspacetime discreteness or complete physicaldynamics.", "whatIsNew": "Representation-levelspectralresults, not demonstratedcosmologicaldynamics.", "limitations": "Abstract-only reading; author-reported result not independently reproduced; full methods/data not reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only; no independentreplicationhere", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "No source data likelihood or apparatus independently reanalysed in this atlas.", "nextQuestions": ["Which statedsystematic,domainorstateassumption is the strongest limitation?", "What additionalindependentdataorcalculation could discriminate the interpretation?"], "title": "Discreteness of area and volume in quantum gravity", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-gwtc5"><data key="title">GWTC-5.0: Tests of General Relativity</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text;source-reportedpreprintresult</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-gwtc5", "sourceId": "grav-src-gwtc5", "topicIds": ["grav-catalogues"], "question": "Whichselectedstrong-field tests andmodeinferences survive statedmodel/systematic assumptions?", "method": "Author waveform/noise/calibration andeventselection analysis; selectedmethods andlimits inspected.", "result": "The2026preprint reports seven selectedGRtests using a cumulative168events under itsselection. It reports no significantbeyond-GR evidence in those tests, while explicitlydiscussing finitecatalogue effects and ringdownsystematics.", "whatIsNew": "Sourceauthors add a newerselectedcatalogue orhigh-SNRsingle-event test. Thisatlas does not certify scientificnovelty.", "limitations": "A selectedpreprint, not an exhaustiveNov2026survey or proof ofGR. Some tests are omitted becauseof knownbiases,weakconstraints orscope. Combinedringdown results include edge-of-credible-region behavior andfinite-sample uncertainty; an overtone can be contaminated by unmodeledcontent.", "status": "selected-text;source-reportedpreprintresult", "equationsUsed": ["grav-f-ringdown"], "replication": "Noindependent strainlikelihood or detector-data replication performed.", "nextQuestions": ["How do baselinewaveforms,eventselection,starttime andnoise models change theconstraint?", "Which modepresence claim is identifiable independently of enforcedmodelstructure?"], "title": "GWTC-5.0: Tests of General Relativity", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-paper-gw250114"><data key="title">Black Hole Spectroscopy and Tests of General Relativity with GW250114</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">selected-text;source-reportedpreprintresult</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-paper-gw250114", "sourceId": "grav-src-gw250114", "topicIds": ["grav-qnm"], "question": "Whichselectedstrong-field tests andmodeinferences survive statedmodel/systematic assumptions?", "method": "Author waveform/noise/calibration andeventselection analysis; selectedmethods andlimits inspected.", "result": "The selected2025preprint reports tests ofGW250114 using ringdown andfull-signal models. It explicitly says its440frequencyconstraint cannot byitself establish that the440mode is present because themodel enforces waveformcontinuity/nonzeroamplitudes.", "whatIsNew": "Sourceauthors add a newerselectedcatalogue orhigh-SNRsingle-event test. Thisatlas does not certify scientificnovelty.", "limitations": "Source-era single-eventclaims,not a continuouslylatestloudestevent assertion. Modepresence,deviationparameters,starttime andwaveformassumptions are distinct. Noindependent detector-data analysis,noise/calibration audit ormode-detection replication here.", "status": "selected-text;source-reportedpreprintresult", "equationsUsed": ["grav-f-ringdown"], "replication": "Noindependent strainlikelihood or detector-data replication performed.", "nextQuestions": ["How do baselinewaveforms,eventselection,starttime andnoise models change theconstraint?", "Which modepresence claim is identifiable independently of enforcedmodelstructure?"], "title": "Black Hole Spectroscopy and Tests of General Relativity with GW250114", "kind": "paper", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-open-1"><data key="title">Is dark energy dynamical rather than a cosmological constant?</data><data key="kind">question</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">unresolved</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-open-1", "question": "Is dark energy dynamical rather than a cosmological constant?", "status": "unresolved", "neededEvidence": "Independentdistance/growth datasets,selection/covariance checks andmodelcomparison robust toSNcalibration andpriors.", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-desi-dr2", "grav-src-desi-dark"], "title": "Is dark energy dynamical rather than a cosmological constant?", "kind": "question", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-open-2"><data key="title">What sources dominate the nanohertz background?</data><data key="kind">question</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><data key="status">unresolved</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "grav-open-2", "question": "What sources dominate the nanohertz background?", "status": "unresolved", "neededEvidence": "Longerbaselines,moreskycoverage,populationmodelcomparison andpossibleindividualsources.", "sourceIds": ["grav-src-pta"], "title": "What sources dominate the nanohertz background?", "kind": "question", "domain": "gravity"}</data></node><node id="grav-open-3"><data key="title">Does a laboratorygravity-relatedentanglement witness uniquely identify a quantum mediator?</data><data key="kind">question</data><data key="domain">gravity</data><dat